  "scope": "S2-47: actual v1 surface-QI and v2/v3/v7 CreateDevice routes carry their creation version before initialization. COLORKEYENABLE is true only for v1; SPECULARENABLE only for v2; NORMALIZENORMALS for v1-v3. Actual initialization and initial sync are tested with non-relevant geometry/material stubs. Initial sync uses the valid Device7 state namespace, preserves SELECTARG1(TEXTURE)/CURRENT and clears zero defaults when reusing the owner host device. Legacy MODULATE alpha selects TEXTURE for ARGB/unbound and CURRENT for RGB; SetTexture recomputes it. Changed legacy stage state opts out; same stage/map values preserve mode; changed map reactivates it. Legacy LIGHTING/LOCALVIEWER/NORMALIZENORMALS return FFFFFFFF and ignore writes while modern getters retain underlying defaults. Modern TEXTUREMAPBLEND rejection/redundant-call behavior is retained. Native actual C verifies 128 RGB/ARGB/unbound cycles, public holds, binding rollback and accepted texture-prefix/alpha-emission retry, plus 170+1052 retained native observations and 20 strict-compiled runtime mutations. XP uses the replacement DLL and Device3/7 views for state and texture calls, not original Microsoft HAL. Sixteen 8x8 ARGB target quads produce actual guest readback commands; CPU replies are simulated, GPU replay independently checks all 1024 RGBA pixels. No fresh Present/game/FPS coverage, general state-block legacy-mode metadata semantics across mixed interfaces, arbitrary formats/Reset/thread/device loss, S2-53 or full review stages 4/5/6 completion. D3D8/9, host/protocol ABI, shaders and bundle are unchanged.",
